WEBVTT

00:00:08.760 --> 00:00:11.940
The leader of the insurgents
that have occupied

00:00:11.940 --> 00:00:13.380
JP's Nagoya Branch is Ronaldo Kuriki.

00:00:13.890 --> 00:00:17.510
He's a former JP's member who
went into hiding two years ago.

00:00:17.720 --> 00:00:20.770
In other words, he's
familiar with our secrets.

00:00:21.850 --> 00:00:25.610
We'll have the train stop 10 kilometers
before Nagoya Station.

00:00:25.990 --> 00:00:27.790
From there, you'll make your way

00:00:27.790 --> 00:00:30.080
aboveground and infiltrate
without getting spotted.

00:00:30.080 --> 00:00:32.490
Once you've helped us
restore the Terminal,

00:00:32.490 --> 00:00:35.080
you're to retake the
Nagoya Branch at once.

00:00:40.000 --> 00:00:42.530
Hey, it worked. Right?

00:00:44.920 --> 00:00:46.120
Success!

00:00:46.260 --> 00:00:50.080
Nitta, stowing away like
this was too bold...

00:00:50.310 --> 00:00:54.640
I-I mean, doing this was our only
way to get to Nagoya, right?

00:00:55.890 --> 00:00:59.480
Friggin' Hibiki. Why would he
leave us and go to Nagoya?

00:00:59.900 --> 00:01:02.710
Maybe he didn't want us to get involved.

00:01:03.280 --> 00:01:04.010
Huh?

00:01:04.360 --> 00:01:06.760
His face. It was scary somehow.

00:01:11.080 --> 00:01:13.650
A friend's "dead face" clip has arrived.

00:01:21.380 --> 00:01:23.200
Well then, have a nice day.

00:01:24.880 --> 00:01:26.080
Hibiki...

00:01:27.180 --> 00:01:28.320
will die?

00:03:10.280 --> 00:03:11.740
Mine won't work either.

00:03:11.740 --> 00:03:15.060
Of all things, a dead
face clip for Hibiki!

00:03:15.700 --> 00:03:17.770
Maybe Makoto and the others got it, too.

00:03:17.910 --> 00:03:21.020
Oh! Ah, no way.

00:03:21.020 --> 00:03:24.450
The dead face clips only go to friends.

00:03:26.840 --> 00:03:30.700
So then... we have to do something!

00:03:33.390 --> 00:03:34.590
How is Nagoya?

00:03:34.930 --> 00:03:36.350
We still can't reach them.

00:03:36.640 --> 00:03:39.020
Communications appear
shut off on their end.

00:03:39.390 --> 00:03:41.940
Communications with the
infiltration unit have ceased.

00:03:42.480 --> 00:03:44.680
So now we're in the dark?

00:03:44.990 --> 00:03:48.090
This is no time for humans to
be fighting one other!

00:03:49.150 --> 00:03:51.220
Hibiki has headed for Nagoya, yes?

00:03:51.490 --> 00:03:54.230
His signal ceased transmitting
once he entered the central area!

00:03:54.570 --> 00:03:56.980
Idiot. So, he was kidnapped?

00:03:58.540 --> 00:04:00.940
We may have pressed him too hard.

00:04:02.910 --> 00:04:05.670
He is a civilian.

00:04:05.670 --> 00:04:08.630
So were you, once. That's no excuse.

00:04:10.050 --> 00:04:12.550
Rank and status are irrelevant.

00:04:13.010 --> 00:04:15.250
We do what we must to
deal with the crisis.

00:04:15.840 --> 00:04:18.540
Whoever can't do that is of no use.

00:04:19.140 --> 00:04:21.800
Still, to have taken Nagoya...

00:04:22.140 --> 00:04:25.710
When the Septentrion appear,
they target our regional barriers.

00:04:26.220 --> 00:04:28.130
And the next one is in Nagoya.

00:04:28.130 --> 00:04:31.810
Yes. According to the binding covenant.

00:04:33.090 --> 00:04:36.360
It seems he, too, has been
pulled into the cogs of fate.

00:04:36.780 --> 00:04:38.560
The cogs of fate?

00:04:39.240 --> 00:04:40.990
How's the Terminal restoration going?

00:04:40.990 --> 00:04:42.580
Prof. Kanno still hasn't-

00:04:42.580 --> 00:04:44.210
Irrelevant. Wake her.

00:04:44.210 --> 00:04:45.450
I'm already on it.

00:04:47.790 --> 00:04:49.530
The program's a mess.

00:04:49.530 --> 00:04:51.210
The backup's been deleted, too.

00:04:51.800 --> 00:04:53.330
By ME, it looks like.

00:04:53.330 --> 00:04:55.630
Fumi, are you all right now?

00:04:55.630 --> 00:04:57.060
Am I not?

00:04:57.060 --> 00:04:59.040
There's no time to lose.

00:04:59.040 --> 00:05:00.600
You're the only one we can turn to.

00:05:00.600 --> 00:05:02.340
I'm rebuilding it from scratch.

00:05:02.720 --> 00:05:03.600
Thank you.

00:05:03.600 --> 00:05:06.410
Sakocchi, why don't you rest a little?

00:05:06.850 --> 00:05:08.400
But, the insurgents...

00:05:08.400 --> 00:05:10.640
The enemy won't show up till tomorrow.

00:05:10.940 --> 00:05:12.060
Rest.

00:05:13.530 --> 00:05:14.940
Sir! You, too.

00:05:14.940 --> 00:05:16.150
Unnecessary.

00:05:19.370 --> 00:05:21.300
Five enemy creatures remain.

00:05:21.970 --> 00:05:23.990
It's only just begun.

00:05:31.290 --> 00:05:35.340
The bureau chief intentionally
sent Hibiki Kuze to Osaka.

00:05:36.260 --> 00:05:38.760
He foresaw Merak's appearance.

00:05:40.140 --> 00:05:41.630
It was foregone.

00:05:42.560 --> 00:05:45.000
Unless we pull through this,
the human race is doomed.

00:05:46.280 --> 00:05:47.310
Two Years Previous

00:05:55.570 --> 00:05:56.560
A kid?

00:05:57.010 --> 00:05:59.370
This kid has been the
power behind the scenes?

00:06:00.700 --> 00:06:04.460
Why... Why was I used?

00:06:04.460 --> 00:06:05.860
I'm a civilian--

00:06:05.860 --> 00:06:07.250
Irrelevant.

00:06:07.910 --> 00:06:10.670
I only acknowledge those with abilities.

00:06:11.080 --> 00:06:13.170
Unlike the other garbage,

00:06:13.170 --> 00:06:14.790
it seems YOU are not incompetent.

00:06:16.010 --> 00:06:18.220
Do you have the resolve...

00:06:18.880 --> 00:06:20.510
to know the world's secret?

00:06:23.220 --> 00:06:26.820
If the bureau chief hadn't recruited me,
I wouldn't be who I am now.

00:06:27.420 --> 00:06:28.580
I...

00:06:29.690 --> 00:06:33.440
I swore I would follow him, didn't I?

00:06:36.400 --> 00:06:38.120
The cogs of fate.

00:06:39.360 --> 00:06:42.660
If all things are in fact
preordained, then why...

00:06:43.160 --> 00:06:48.230
Why is humanity able
to think for itself?

00:06:52.420 --> 00:06:56.180
If Prof. Kanno is back, we
can restore the barriers

00:06:56.180 --> 00:06:58.420
and prevent others like Merak, can't we?

00:06:58.420 --> 00:07:00.500
I hope that's the case...

00:07:01.340 --> 00:07:02.550
Is it ready?

00:07:02.550 --> 00:07:05.750
Sir! There's still much
we don't understand...

00:07:06.390 --> 00:07:07.720
It just has to work.

00:07:07.720 --> 00:07:08.630
It can.

00:07:29.410 --> 00:07:30.660
Jungo...

00:07:31.580 --> 00:07:34.130
Ah! When did I fall asleep?!

00:07:34.130 --> 00:07:36.000
It can't be helped. You were tired.

00:07:36.000 --> 00:07:38.030
I said this is no time
for sleeping, right?!

00:07:38.250 --> 00:07:40.160
The second you said it, you were asleep.

00:07:42.730 --> 00:07:44.910
It's all right. I slept, too.

00:07:45.510 --> 00:07:48.080
Okay! Our demons are all restored, too.

00:07:48.080 --> 00:07:51.380
Well, time to take JP's
back from the insurgents!

00:07:52.020 --> 00:07:53.310
It's dangerous on your own.

00:07:53.310 --> 00:07:54.770
YOU'RE going, too!

00:07:55.110 --> 00:07:55.680
Me?

00:07:56.150 --> 00:07:58.840
Jeez, you're seriously messed up.

00:07:58.840 --> 00:08:02.720
All the others were captured,
and communications won't work.

00:08:03.200 --> 00:08:04.990
Our only choice is for
the two of us to do it!

00:08:05.630 --> 00:08:06.440
But first...

00:08:07.330 --> 00:08:09.650
Eat some chawanmushi.
You'll feel better.

00:08:11.830 --> 00:08:13.960
You're pretty nonchalant, huh?

00:08:18.090 --> 00:08:19.370
It's delicious.

00:08:19.590 --> 00:08:22.470
I'm glad. Say, Airi...

00:08:23.720 --> 00:08:25.580
Do we have to side with JP's?

00:08:26.090 --> 00:08:27.720
What do you mean?

00:08:27.720 --> 00:08:30.600
They're scary somehow.
Too many mysteries.

00:08:30.600 --> 00:08:32.650
I'm grateful for being rescued, but...

00:08:33.060 --> 00:08:35.590
the way they talked like
they knew the disaster

00:08:35.590 --> 00:08:37.340
would happen was weird, huh?

00:08:37.520 --> 00:08:40.880
Also, no matter who we side with,

00:08:40.880 --> 00:08:42.810
I don't want human to fight human.

00:08:43.360 --> 00:08:45.160
You're pretty wishy-washy, aren't you?

00:08:45.160 --> 00:08:47.350
Why not go and ask for yourself?

00:08:47.660 --> 00:08:49.330
Ask whom? About what?

00:08:49.330 --> 00:08:50.960
The insurgents' leader!

00:08:50.960 --> 00:08:52.820
It looks like those guys

00:08:53.300 --> 00:08:57.200
knew about JP's and the demons from the start.

00:08:58.250 --> 00:08:59.820
What should I do?

00:09:00.170 --> 00:09:03.690
We're gonna use that secret route
the insurgents don't know about.

00:09:05.260 --> 00:09:06.720
Airi, on your mouth.

00:09:06.720 --> 00:09:07.790
Hey!

00:09:22.690 --> 00:09:24.600
It's pretty bad here too, huh?

00:09:25.200 --> 00:09:25.970
Yes.

00:09:25.970 --> 00:09:27.180
Okay!

00:09:27.740 --> 00:09:31.270
Nitta, uh, which way is the
Nagoya Branch again?

00:09:31.910 --> 00:09:36.820
Oh. Makoto said to go underground,
beneath Centering Park.

00:09:37.000 --> 00:09:38.380
Is that so?

00:09:38.960 --> 00:09:41.550
Speaking of, she didn't try to stop you?

00:09:41.550 --> 00:09:43.500
No, just the opposite.

00:09:44.260 --> 00:09:46.330
Makoto turned a blind eye, huh?

00:09:46.630 --> 00:09:50.390
I think our not getting
caught on the train

00:09:50.390 --> 00:09:52.620
was also thanks to her guidance.

00:09:53.520 --> 00:09:55.430
I thought she was scary...

00:09:56.310 --> 00:10:00.110
If it hadn't been for this,
they'd all be good people, huh?

00:10:08.280 --> 00:10:09.880
Huh? What's this?

00:10:10.450 --> 00:10:12.650
It's not the police or JP's, is it?

00:10:12.650 --> 00:10:14.040
Civilians?

00:10:14.040 --> 00:10:14.670
Hey!

00:10:15.290 --> 00:10:16.450
What're you doin'?

00:10:17.460 --> 00:10:19.420
Take it. Here's yours.

00:10:20.580 --> 00:10:21.290
Um...

00:10:21.290 --> 00:10:22.040
Thanks.

00:10:22.040 --> 00:10:24.500
Even with things like this,
they're not sendin' aid.

00:10:24.500 --> 00:10:26.330
We can't trust the government or no one!

00:10:27.170 --> 00:10:29.630
WE'LL run things goin'
forward, so we'll be fine.

00:10:30.260 --> 00:10:31.590
Thank you very much.

00:10:31.590 --> 00:10:33.220
See ya. Take care.

00:10:35.430 --> 00:10:38.630
Huh? Aren't these JP's rations?

00:10:38.630 --> 00:10:41.720
You're right. These guys stole them?

00:10:46.570 --> 00:10:48.970
Okay, okay. There's enough for everyone.

00:10:49.400 --> 00:10:51.740
These people... are insurgents?

00:10:57.450 --> 00:10:58.370
Demons!

00:10:59.960 --> 00:11:02.210
Hey! Go get someone who can use demons!

00:11:03.290 --> 00:11:04.780
Just leave this to me!

00:11:05.050 --> 00:11:06.700
Go, my demons!

00:11:07.460 --> 00:11:08.470
Obariyon!

00:11:08.880 --> 00:11:09.700
Agathion!

00:11:14.010 --> 00:11:16.500
My demons are weak!

00:11:16.810 --> 00:11:17.750
Kikuri-Hime!

00:11:22.770 --> 00:11:24.730
N-Nitta, you're so tough...

00:11:25.650 --> 00:11:26.900
Did it.

00:11:26.900 --> 00:11:29.220
Poltergeist, put out the fires.

00:11:33.370 --> 00:11:35.730
Hey. You guys are Summoners, too?

00:11:35.910 --> 00:11:37.240
This look bad...

00:11:37.240 --> 00:11:38.540
Don't you move!

00:11:39.680 --> 00:11:40.730
There's so many of 'em!

00:11:41.080 --> 00:11:43.240
How long is this gonna go on?

00:11:43.630 --> 00:11:46.070
Um... This isn't good, right?

00:11:58.010 --> 00:11:59.020
Hibiki!

00:11:59.020 --> 00:12:01.320
Thank goodness. You made us worry, fool!

00:12:01.320 --> 00:12:02.410
Mr. Hibiki!

00:12:04.730 --> 00:12:06.590
Suzaku. Burn them.

00:12:10.030 --> 00:12:11.490
A-Awesome...

00:12:13.110 --> 00:12:15.850
Hibiki! Hibiki! Hibiki!

00:12:16.370 --> 00:12:18.560
We saw your dead face!

00:12:21.910 --> 00:12:25.080
Hey! That's Hibiki, right?
Where'd he go?

00:12:25.330 --> 00:12:26.750
Who the hell are you?

00:12:26.750 --> 00:12:29.980
I'm his friend! Tell me!

00:12:29.980 --> 00:12:32.920
Mr. Hibiki will probably see the leader.

00:12:33.470 --> 00:12:34.840
Take us there.

00:12:35.930 --> 00:12:39.080
Please take us there!

00:13:00.080 --> 00:13:02.110
For you all to do this...

00:13:02.110 --> 00:13:04.190
You understand the situation, don't you?

00:13:04.500 --> 00:13:06.510
Demons appeared, right?

00:13:06.510 --> 00:13:08.660
Then everything went to hell.

00:13:09.000 --> 00:13:13.050
You all knew this would happen,
yet you abandoned the civilians!

00:13:13.050 --> 00:13:17.510
No. Not abandoned. We--

00:13:17.510 --> 00:13:19.440
That's wrong!

00:13:19.440 --> 00:13:20.920
You don't know anything!

00:13:21.180 --> 00:13:23.270
Yeah, we don't know anything.

00:13:23.730 --> 00:13:27.360
Can YOU all say that to those
who've died none the wiser?!

00:13:27.850 --> 00:13:29.260
Leave them alone.

00:13:29.810 --> 00:13:31.760
Ronaldo. Mr. Hibiki.

00:13:32.440 --> 00:13:35.220
They just obeyed the
orders they were given.

00:13:35.990 --> 00:13:37.570
You're the insurgents' leader?

00:13:39.120 --> 00:13:40.560
Ronaldo!

00:13:40.950 --> 00:13:44.350
What we have to stop is
Yamato Hotsuin alone.

00:13:44.350 --> 00:13:46.260
The bureau chief... alone?

00:13:46.670 --> 00:13:49.340
The circuit to contact JP's has
been rendered inoperable.

00:13:49.830 --> 00:13:51.900
But you're a Summoner, too.

00:13:51.900 --> 00:13:54.130
You need that to protect others.

00:13:54.130 --> 00:13:56.160
What you're doing is terrorism!

00:13:56.630 --> 00:14:00.550
Unless we defeat seven Septentrion,
mankind will die.

00:14:01.030 --> 00:14:03.750
That's what Yamato Hotsuin says.

00:14:04.840 --> 00:14:06.420
Sept... Die?

00:14:06.770 --> 00:14:09.440
So, you know the situation.

00:14:09.440 --> 00:14:10.360
Yes.

00:14:10.360 --> 00:14:13.610
Then why would you occupy JP's?!

00:14:13.610 --> 00:14:18.110
Once Yamato Hotsuin beats the Septentrion,
he'll institute a meritocracy.

00:14:18.530 --> 00:14:21.390
He will be the leader of the new world.

00:14:21.870 --> 00:14:23.770
For him, our current situation

00:14:23.770 --> 00:14:26.400
is a chance to make good
on his own ambitions.

00:14:27.290 --> 00:14:31.320
Yamato has manipulated both JP's
and the Japanese government.

00:14:31.320 --> 00:14:34.090
True, the chief is a
little scary, but...

00:14:34.090 --> 00:14:35.660
What's your proof?

00:14:36.410 --> 00:14:37.830
I'm a former detective!

00:14:38.470 --> 00:14:41.520
The government scouted
me for my achievements,

00:14:41.520 --> 00:14:43.170
and I became a member of JP's.

00:14:43.600 --> 00:14:45.350
A JP's COMP...

00:14:45.350 --> 00:14:47.100
A curse of the job.

00:14:47.100 --> 00:14:49.170
Once there, I did a lot of snooping...

00:14:50.350 --> 00:14:53.980
Into the greatest secret in history:
the mystery of the Hotsuin family.

00:14:54.610 --> 00:14:59.180
And when I learned the true intent of
its current head, he tried to kill me.

00:14:59.860 --> 00:15:02.940
"If you won't obey, you
are useless," he said.

00:15:03.410 --> 00:15:05.840
Mr. Hibiki, did you know that?!

00:15:06.370 --> 00:15:08.120
He's a cunning man.

00:15:08.120 --> 00:15:11.810
In following him, you were
made into his machine.

00:15:12.210 --> 00:15:16.070
"Even if it's as his machine, if
doing it is the right thing, then..."

00:15:16.900 --> 00:15:18.160
That's what I thought.

00:15:18.160 --> 00:15:19.700
There's nothing "right" about it.

00:15:20.340 --> 00:15:23.370
His methods will lead those
without power to die.

00:15:23.850 --> 00:15:26.960
Remember that scene,
what happened around you.

00:15:33.310 --> 00:15:37.350
I can't accept the world a man
like THAT would make.

00:15:37.820 --> 00:15:39.010
All people...

00:15:39.490 --> 00:15:40.630
are equal.

00:15:44.780 --> 00:15:46.830
Hurry up and help me!

00:15:47.880 --> 00:15:48.860
I'll help.

00:15:52.440 --> 00:15:54.880
The heck? That was easy for you to open!

00:15:54.880 --> 00:15:55.710
Sorry.

00:15:57.050 --> 00:15:58.590
It would be tight for me.

00:15:58.590 --> 00:16:00.870
No complaints. We're going!

00:16:02.970 --> 00:16:04.680
To think, he's an egalitarian...

00:16:05.510 --> 00:16:07.540
Is that even possible?

00:16:07.810 --> 00:16:13.050
Huh? The stuff Ronaldo says?
I don't really get it.

00:16:13.650 --> 00:16:17.050
Then why are you a member
of the resistance, Joe?

00:16:18.570 --> 00:16:20.490
That's how it turned out.

00:16:20.490 --> 00:16:23.870
If the government knew
about this but kept quiet,

00:16:23.870 --> 00:16:25.310
it'd piss you off, right?

00:16:25.620 --> 00:16:28.200
Like, "You just turn your
backs on us civilians?"

00:16:28.200 --> 00:16:31.320
Well, the world ain't fair
at all right now, huh?

00:16:33.420 --> 00:16:35.000
Yes, you're right.

00:16:35.200 --> 00:16:37.840
Huh? You're kinda gloomy.

00:16:38.240 --> 00:16:40.350
At least you're alive.

00:16:40.350 --> 00:16:42.450
Folks who aren't hurt can't be gloomy.

00:16:45.340 --> 00:16:47.430
You gotta live cheerfully!

00:16:48.010 --> 00:16:49.670
THAT was cheering me up?

00:16:50.270 --> 00:16:52.590
He lost his girlfriend to all this.

00:16:52.590 --> 00:16:53.340
Huh?

00:16:54.690 --> 00:16:56.350
Everyone's been hurt.

00:16:56.810 --> 00:16:59.010
Hibiki, will you come with me?

00:17:03.440 --> 00:17:05.020
You've penetrated this far?

00:17:05.740 --> 00:17:09.020
Luckily, we have plenty of
powerful Summoners, too.

00:17:09.410 --> 00:17:13.470
Who intentionally gave
us the summoning app?

00:17:14.210 --> 00:17:16.500
We're looking into that ourselves.

00:17:17.130 --> 00:17:19.030
If we learn who developed it,

00:17:19.030 --> 00:17:21.120
we definitely want to welcome them as friends.

00:17:23.330 --> 00:17:23.990
We're here.

00:17:24.880 --> 00:17:26.500
This is our temporary command center.

00:17:30.470 --> 00:17:33.880
Ronaldo. That's the cutie you
snatched from Osaka, huh?

00:17:34.350 --> 00:17:35.460
That's right.

00:17:35.460 --> 00:17:38.880
This young man is the most
powerful confirmed Summoner.

00:17:40.480 --> 00:17:43.060
Byakko AND Suzaku? Scary!

00:17:43.060 --> 00:17:45.100
Not even your Hagen could beat that.

00:17:46.740 --> 00:17:48.100
That's why we're counting on him.

00:17:48.740 --> 00:17:50.030
Thanks for your help!

00:17:50.740 --> 00:17:52.790
Let's begin, Hibiki.

00:17:53.500 --> 00:17:54.580
Listen carefully.

00:17:55.500 --> 00:17:58.600
If the lore of the Hotsuin
family is correct,

00:17:58.600 --> 00:18:02.460
a Septentrion will appear
here in Nagoya, today.

00:18:03.340 --> 00:18:05.770
We won't let it just
appear like in Osaka.

00:18:05.770 --> 00:18:08.000
We're well prepared, y'know.

00:18:08.220 --> 00:18:09.590
Unlike SOME branches,

00:18:09.590 --> 00:18:11.160
we won't have control taken from us

00:18:11.160 --> 00:18:13.630
and manifestation rate increase tenfold.

00:18:14.640 --> 00:18:17.110
If we want the resistance to be known

00:18:17.110 --> 00:18:18.840
and make ourselves a powerful force,

00:18:18.840 --> 00:18:20.610
it has to be US,

00:18:20.610 --> 00:18:23.100
not the government or JP's,
who defeats the enemy.

00:18:23.530 --> 00:18:25.870
And we can do it.

00:18:26.720 --> 00:18:27.640
How's that?

00:18:28.280 --> 00:18:31.320
My Hagen. And your Byakko and Suzaku.

00:18:31.320 --> 00:18:32.900
And my Orcus.

00:18:34.040 --> 00:18:35.370
And her...

00:18:35.370 --> 00:18:36.520
Sarasvati.

00:18:37.080 --> 00:18:38.280
You're from JP's?

00:18:39.040 --> 00:18:41.320
The Septentrion are coming, right?

00:18:41.320 --> 00:18:43.280
We have to cooperate, don't we?

00:18:43.920 --> 00:18:46.540
It's not as if I've joined you.

00:18:47.470 --> 00:18:49.590
I feel badly for getting you involved.

00:18:50.390 --> 00:18:52.930
We'll keep the enemy's
manifestation rate to a minimum,

00:18:52.930 --> 00:18:55.030
and have a powerful battle formation.

00:18:55.520 --> 00:18:56.750
We're plenty good to fight!

00:18:57.350 --> 00:18:59.480
This person really plans to do it.

00:19:00.310 --> 00:19:03.380
And we will sacrifice no one.

00:19:03.820 --> 00:19:06.940
True, whoever CAN fight
the Septentrion will do.

00:19:06.940 --> 00:19:12.890
Also, I bet these people wouldn't
use others as human shields.

00:19:13.530 --> 00:19:16.390
They're weak, all of them.

00:19:16.790 --> 00:19:19.360
They can be broken, they
flock like sheep...

00:19:19.830 --> 00:19:22.400
The incompetent should
be recognized as such.

00:19:22.960 --> 00:19:25.060
There is no future for the weak.

00:19:25.590 --> 00:19:29.840
Which is precisely why the
strong must take lead.

00:19:54.410 --> 00:19:56.780
Mr. Yamato. Today, we continue our

00:19:56.780 --> 00:19:59.070
study of this outline
on atomic energy...

00:19:59.120 --> 00:20:01.460
You're still going on about that?

00:20:02.080 --> 00:20:06.320
I mastered it long ago.
You are of no use.

00:20:06.960 --> 00:20:09.260
Scum. You may go.

00:20:15.510 --> 00:20:18.890
For a supposed grandmaster of tea ceremony,
that was nothing special.

00:20:19.520 --> 00:20:20.590
Make more when we get back.

00:20:22.190 --> 00:20:24.440
Did it not suit your palate?

00:20:25.860 --> 00:20:27.080
Hey, welcome.

00:20:27.570 --> 00:20:28.620
What's that?

00:20:28.900 --> 00:20:32.340
That sort of thing wouldn't
suit your tastes.

00:20:33.360 --> 00:20:34.360
I see.

00:20:40.980 --> 00:20:42.150
Data measurement is impossible!

00:20:42.150 --> 00:20:43.030
Shut it down!

00:20:44.960 --> 00:20:46.900
They all frighten too much.

00:20:47.460 --> 00:20:49.690
Nothing has even started yet.

00:20:50.550 --> 00:20:51.280
How boring.

00:20:57.180 --> 00:20:58.540
This is... Impossible!

00:20:59.510 --> 00:21:00.710
It's Cerberus!

00:21:01.810 --> 00:21:05.720
That demon can't be called on a
first summoning! Or by a kid!

00:21:07.480 --> 00:21:08.360
The system is down.

00:21:08.360 --> 00:21:09.840
Cerberus can't be controlled!

00:21:10.440 --> 00:21:13.120
It's far surpassed previous levels!

00:21:13.120 --> 00:21:14.460
You monster!

00:21:14.460 --> 00:21:15.270
Secure it!

00:21:18.330 --> 00:21:19.430
Enough.

00:21:29.960 --> 00:21:31.320
Such power!

00:21:33.670 --> 00:21:34.790
Incompetent.

00:21:51.400 --> 00:21:52.510
I've found you.

00:21:52.940 --> 00:21:54.440
O Sparkling One.

00:22:01.790 --> 00:22:03.190
Check, isn't it?

00:22:03.680 --> 00:22:04.940
Don't be foolish.

00:22:05.410 --> 00:22:06.690
I've kept the rules.

00:22:07.500 --> 00:22:10.200
I don't recall admitting
defeat to the likes of YOU.

00:22:11.340 --> 00:22:13.340
This is a difficult game.

00:22:13.340 --> 00:22:14.710
One more time.

00:22:14.710 --> 00:22:17.090
Fine. One more time.

00:22:28.650 --> 00:22:32.570
The game has only just begun, Alcor.

00:22:32.900 --> 00:22:33.860
That's right.

00:22:34.360 --> 00:22:36.810
But the Sparkling One is no longer here.

00:22:37.450 --> 00:22:40.810
This ideal you were
after has never existed.

00:22:41.400 --> 00:22:42.560
What do you mean?

00:22:42.780 --> 00:22:45.410
It's STRENGTH that shapes the world.

00:22:45.950 --> 00:22:48.440
Those of ability should simply lead.

00:22:49.000 --> 00:22:50.700
Are there no other possibilities?

00:22:50.920 --> 00:22:51.850
None.

00:22:52.840 --> 00:22:54.610
Let me prove it.

00:22:58.720 --> 00:23:00.580
Yamato. You don't change.

00:23:01.090 --> 00:23:03.330
Nor you. It's appalling.

00:23:03.930 --> 00:23:05.320
It's almost time, isn't it?

00:23:05.720 --> 00:23:06.890
Indeed.

00:23:07.730 --> 00:23:09.770
And Hibiki? You think he can win?

00:23:14.920 --> 00:23:17.560
A friend's "dead face" clip has arrived.

00:23:18.360 --> 00:23:20.180
Friend, you say?
